# W - Ugur interatomic potential, CANDIDATE, re-cut, switched, with the angular factor
#
# pair_style ugur/ang
# pair_coeff * * W_recut.ugur.ang W
#
# Truncation: switched from 0.85 of each cutoff to the cutoff, quintic, C2 - energy is conserved in MD.  CANDIDATE: the angular re-cut is never the recommended set.  Its dispersion advantage is mostly the alkalis, which it breaks warm; read the notes below before using it
# MD: structure screened - holds its shape at 600 K (308 K, as equipartition requires).  This tested the SHAPE, not energy conservation; for that see the truncation line above.
#
# LATTICE STABILITY: this set is NOT a harmonic minimum.
# Along the Setyawan-Curtarolo path its frequencies reach -8.215 cm^-1,
# with 0.15 % of the sampled modes imaginary.  That is a separate
# failure from the 600 K screen above and is not covered by it.
#
# Nudge test: passed - displaced by 1e-5 A and relaxed, the lattice returns.
#
# Measured dispersion: 17.2 % against 17.8 % for the published switched
# arm - better.
# Over the 20 accepted angular re-cut records: thermal expansion error
# 35.0 % -> 34.7 % median, 11 better and 8 worse; elastic constants near 300 K
# against the room-temperature values 3.7 % -> 3.4 % median, 9 better and 11 worse.
#
# REJECTED: this record did NOT pass selection -
# it carries a mode at -8.2 cm^-1 on the symmetry path; it puts fcc lowest, 432 meV/atom below bcc.
# It is kept as the control the accepted records are read against,
# not as a potential.  Do not use it.
#
# Fitted to: cohesive energy, lattice constant, bulk modulus and the elastic
# constants of W at its experimental lattice constant.  Nothing else.
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
